  "summary": "Polish Impressionism was an art movement inspired by French Impressionism.",
  "description": "Polish Impressionism was an art movement inspired by French Impressionism. Władysław Podkowiński is generally credited with introducing the movement to Poland after a trip to Paris in 1889, where he was profoundly influenced by French Impressionist painters including Claude Monet. Toward the end of his life, however, he turned more toward Symbolism. Olga Boznańska is possibly the most well known Polish Impressionist, recognized in London and Paris, and winning many prizes. The French Government purchased two of her works.",
